<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>63.0</apiVersion>
    <description>Fraud Alert Flow (ECRMSF-5511 / ECRMSF-5529, tasks 10/11). Fires on new Submission-type Application_Login__c rows. Evaluates the Shared IP 30-day count against an admin-tunable threshold (setting Shared_IP_Warning__c), then evaluates all three fraud signals together - Shared_IP_Warning__c, IP_Location_Match_Warning__c (set separately by the Location_Match_Warning Flow, which runs first since Flows on the same trigger fire in a defined order), and a below-threshold Scored reCAPTCHA score on this specific submission event. If any signal is tripped, sets Fraud_Review_Status__c to &quot;Review Recommended&quot; (only when currently blank, so staff already reviewing an application are never silently reset) and sends an email alert to the admin-configured recipient list. This Flow never blocks or denies the application - monitoring/staff-review only. See docs/fraud-monitoring-recaptcha-ip-geo.md for full design rationale.</description>
